```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_FAILED",
    "message": "One or more fields failed validation",
    "retryable": false,
    "details": [
      { "field": "email", "issue": "must be a valid email address" },
      { "field": "age", "issue": "must be a positive integer" }
    ]
  }
}
```

Every endpoint in the service — regardless of team or which resource it's about — returns exactly this envelope shape on failure, with only `code`, `message`, `retryable`, and `details`'s contents varying. A shared middleware or error-handling layer, not each endpoint's own logic, is what typically enforces this consistently.
